    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0877" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/11–2345</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-23">November 23,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received December 5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to our despatch
                    No. 56, November 14, 1945, and to previous correspondence on the subject of
                    official relations between the Japanese Government and neutral nations. There is
                    enclosed a copy of a directive dated November 18, 1945, to the Japanese
                        Government<anchor n="36" xml:id="d622-f1"/> in which a request that Japanese
                    Liaison Officers be permitted to supervise the routine functions of Switzerland
                    and Sweden in the protection of Japanese nationals in neutral countries is
                    denied. The Japanese Government is also directed to report immediately the steps
                    taken to comply with the memorandum of October 25, 1945,<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d622-f2"/> a copy of which was forwarded to the Department with our
                    despatch under reference.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Atcheson, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
